# UNLZH - Restore a CrLZH file

```text
UNLZH [drive:]file [destination-drive:]
```

## Restore a file

```text
B0:UNLZH A:REPORT.TYT D:
```

The original filename comes from the CrLZH header. Choose a drive with
room and a free destination name. A checksum or stream error prevents
publication of the restored file.

## Historical files

UNLZH recognizes supported old (10h) and new (20h) CrLZH variants from
their headers. Use [LZH](LZH.HLP) to make a new compressed copy. Use
[UNCR](UNCR.HLP) for CRUNCH 2.x files.
